{"ts": "2026-11-06T21:15:00", "task": "Skill System gaps 2-4: reactive Skills, partner draft rule, client draft test", "status": "ok", "note": "Closed the three remaining Skill System gaps. GAP 2 (5 unconsumed Skill kinds): SK-008 Luck LV.2 / SK-010 Toughness LV.1 / SK-012 Toughness LV.3 are implemented as DECLARED reactions (new PendingSkillEffect kinds negateNextDamage / negateNextInfectedEffect / redirectNextInfectedEffect, armed through the existing useSkill action, consumed by consumeNegateDamage / consumeInfectedEffectReaction which also remove the Skill's XP as the printed cost). The engine cannot interrupt a resolved combat, so the reaction must be armed before the triggering event - documented in types.ts. SK-008 is consumed at the infected-attack damage, the MA-037/MA-031 AoE reveal damage, and the pendingExplore (Jill flash-grenade) resolution; SK-010/012 at the onReveal / onDefeat / onNotDefeated infection-increase and skip-turn / no-actions effect sites. SK-009 Luck LV.3 now actually does something: activeSkillEffects appends the other active Skills' effects a second time so a copied passive stacks (SK-009 + SK-011 = -20 damage). SK-029 Handgun Technique LV.2 is a turn-start 'can' Skill: new turnStartSkillPrompts offers Reveal 2 Pistols -> +1 Explore (wired into startTurn next to turnStartAbilityPrompts). GAP 3: new client 'Mercenaries Skill draft UI' describe (3 tests) asserts the draft prompt renders the seat's five Skill NAMES (never raw instance ids), that sanitize() hides the other seat's draft hand, and that a pick advances the draft. GAP 4: SkillDraftState.keepTarget (3, or 2 with the Partner Modification) drives the keep step and the prompt text; finishDraft assigns the second kept Skill to the partner (PlayerState.partnerSkillId) and the SkillPanel badges it 'Partner'; a partner reduced to 0 Health now dies and its Skill + XP are Removed (removePartnerSkill). Tests: +7 game-core (SK-008/009/010/012/029 x2 + partner draft = 17 in skill.test.ts) and +3 client. Gates: typecheck exit 0, game-core 550, server 96, client 131, client vite build OK. KNOWN LIMITATION: the reactive Skills are armed before the event rather than reacted to at the moment of the event, and SK-010/012 cover the infection-increase / turn-penalty / AoE effects applied in actions.ts - combat-modifying infected effects resolved inside the pure resolveExplore() (onRevealWeaponDamagePenalty, onRevealHealthPenaltyIfMultipleWeapons, cannotBeDefeatedIf*) are not yet interceptable."}
{"ts": "2026-11-06T22:40:00", "task": "Outbreak Infected Characters CH-031/032/033 implemented + pendingExplore stale-snapshot fix", "status": "ok", "note": "Added the three Infected Characters from Manny's card data. Data (outbreak.ts): ch-031 Zombie A (HP 140, baseDamage 0), ch-032 Zombie B (HP 140 - was wrongly 150 - baseDamage 5), ch-033 Zombie C (HP 140, baseDamage 10), all with verbatim text + a level-1 ability. New CharacterAbility kinds: zombieAAoEOnAttack (A: when it attacks, all other non-infected characters not being attacked take 10), zombieBInfectionIncrease (B: trash an infection card from hand to raise the affected character's level by 1 more), zombieCTurnStartInfectionSwap (C: turn start, move a hand infection to the bottom of the Infection Deck and take the top card into hand). Engine: AoE in the attack handler; B via a new zombieBPrompts() queued at every effect-driven infection increase (attack infectionIncrease, onReveal/onRevealAll/onDefeat/onNotDefeated infection increases) and resolved by trashing an infection card to draw a fresh one onto the affected character; C via turnStartAbilityPrompts + a chooseOption handler. Reanimate now recomputes the Character's level with levelForDecorations so the zombie abilities are actually level-gated in. FIXED a real latent conservation bug the soak caught: the Jill flash-grenade pendingExplore resolution restored the saved seat/mansion/rng SNAPSHOT, silently discarding everything that happened while the reactive prompt was open (alliance/2 orphaned we-004#s1_2 - the exploring player kept playing ammo/actions and ending the turn, then the restore put the card back in a play area that the next startTurn cleared). It now applies only the combat OUTCOME to the CURRENT state: decorations via a new pendingExplore.decorationDelta, HP from the current seat, the revealed Infected to removed/bottom of the CURRENT mansion deck, and the current rngState. Also fixed zombieBPrompts being built from the pre-attack state (it offered an infection card the attacker had just discarded). Tests: +4 outbreak (Zombie A AoE, Zombie B accept, Zombie B decline, Zombie C swap). Gates: typecheck exit 0, game-core 554, server 96, client 131, client vite build OK; soak natural-end rate improved 18/27 -> 19/27."}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T00:10:00", "task": "Mercenaries expansion: implement all 52 remaining card effects", "status": "ok", "note": "Encoded + implemented the 52 data-only Mercenaries cards (8 characters, 8 weapons, 10 actions, 26 infected). Data: every effect is machine-readable (no generic no-ops). Engine: new engine/mercenaries.ts (reveal/defeat/not-defeated/on-defeat entry points + gainAmmoX10/gainCopy/dealDamageToCharacter/removeInstanceEverywhere/ownerSeatOf/decorationDelta) and engine/ammo.ts (exploreAmmoReq/requiredAmmoForExplore centralise the Ammo Requirement math). types.ts: new PlayerState fields, useWeaponAbility action, CH-044..051/WE-043..050/AC-042..051/MA-073..098 kinds, fightOrFlight reactive window, pendingExplore fields. Wired actions.ts/explore.ts/game.ts/validate.ts/ai/enumerate.ts; client ActionBar weapon-ability buttons + turnHistory label. Fixes: reveal/not-defeated prompts were never merged into state (MA-076/080/086/089/090 prompts were lost); HUNK's on-damage Ammo x10 gain was missing; MA-092 reveal gains were overwritten by the explore's seat updates (now deferred); MA-077 Chicken's 'worth 0 Decorations while in a Combo Pile by itself' applied via decorationDelta (lone MA-077 adds 0, attaching another restores its 3); MA-078 now subtracts the moved Infected's Decoration reward. Tests: new engine/mercenaries.test.ts (49, one per card). Gates: typecheck exit 0, game-core 603, server 131, client 96, client vite build OK, soak green. Known limitation: Mercenary Mode team/combo/timer rules are out of scope, so MA-077 is applied to the base engine's attached-Infected list."}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T08:20:00", "task": "Nightmare expansion: implement all 50 cards (data + engine + scenario)", "status": "ok", "note": "Encoded + implemented the 50 Nightmare cards (10 characters CH-034..043, 11 weapons WE-032..042, 16 infected MA-054..069, 2 items MA-070/071, 1 event MA-072, 10 actions AC-032..041) from the official RE4 rulebook PDF (docs/rules/nightmare/RE4_Rulebook.pdf) + wiki card scans + the Master Card List xls. Data: every effect is machine-readable (no generic no-ops); CH-034 is single-level. New engine/nightmare.ts (applyNightmareRevealEffects / DefeatEffects / NotDefeatedEffects / nightmareWeaponGains / nightmareWeaponPrompts / applyMindControlCopy). types.ts: new CharacterAbility/WeaponEffect/InfectedEffect/ActionEffect kinds, removeAttachedItem action, PlayerState fields. New 'nightmare' scenario: NIGHTMARE_PILES (23 piles) + NIGHTMARE_MANSION (MA-054..MA-072) + winInfectedCardId 'ma-054' (Osmund Saddler), wired through setup/host/hotseat/sim; ScenarioId, EXPANSION_SCENARIOS, SCENARIOS, ALL_CARDS, protocol whitelist updated. Client: ActionBar renders attached-item removal buttons; turnHistory label. ENGINE FIXES found by the new tests + soak: (1) resolveExplore was never passed the params the Nightmare reveal effects read - characterAbilities (Chris L1 +10 vs 40+ HP), actionsInPlayArea (MA-062), inventoryCount (MA-065), characterDamage (MA-067), ammoCardsInPlayArea (WE-034), infectedBattledThisTurn (WE-042); (2) the explore defeat/not-defeated branches rebuilt the exploring seat from the PRE-reveal snapshot, silently discarding MA-061's reveal damage and MA-068's max-HP reduction - the seat is now re-read after the reveal effects; (3) grantedExplores was only applied on the non-infected branch, so WE-040 Flashbang's +1 Explore never fired; (4) MA-057 Jack Krauser gained the pile's top card without popping it (gainCard with an instanceId only relocates the instance) - duplicate instance; (5) the P.R.L. 412 auto-defeat attached ONE Infect