{"ts": "2026-11-07T11:08:13", "task": "Wire flipDown/downing into the damage path (+ Outbreak out-of-game rules)", "status": "ok", "note": "flipDown/revive existed in engine/characters.ts but flipDown was imported into actions.ts and never called, so a character at 0 Health kept taking turns (the attack path even subtracted HP unclamped, so seats went to -75). Added an applyDownedHooks choke point in engine/actions.ts that runs after EVERY action and downs any seat at <=0 Health: hand+discard shuffled into the Inventory, both emptied, attached cards kept, hp clamped to 0. The explore path keeps its inline down because AC-050 Resuscitate intercepts it; the hook skips already-downed seats. Outbreak out-of-game rules: validate.ts rejects any action started by a downed Character (only endTurn/chooseOption stay legal), rejects attacking a downed target, and every 'choose another player' prompt, the reactive trash windows, the end-of-turn 'all characters' infection increase, the Wesker/Rebecca/force-explore ability targets, the bot's attack enumeration and useCharacterAbility validation now exclude downed seats; the end-of-turn Infection increase also skips downed Characters. revive (startTurn) was already correct: -20 max Health, heal to the new max, draw 5 with reshuffle, skip the turn, permanent defeat at <=0 max Health. New engine/downed.test.ts (8 tests): attack downs, attached cards stay, revive, permanent defeat at 20 max HP, cannot be attacked, no Infection rise, idempotent, out-of-game action ban. Gates: typecheck exit 0 (3 workspaces), game-core 666, server 96, client 131, client vite build OK, soak green (23/30 natural, was 24/30 before the dedup - downing shortens some games, no stalls)."}
