{"ts": "2026-11-07T14:59:51", "task": "Multi-explore (exploreCount) + Partner Modification explore fix", "status": "ok", "note": "Rulebook 'Extra Explore' is now implemented: an explore action carries exploreCount (1..exploresLeft, capped by deckCount(mansionDeck+mansionBottom)); the engine reveals N cards one at a time and battles ALL revealed Infected as ONE combined engagement (total damage vs combined HP, failure = combined damage, every undefeated Infected to the bottom/shuffle-back). resolveMultiExplore was extended to apply every per-card on-reveal combat effect (onRevealPlusHpPerSameNameAttached, onRevealPlusHpPerAttachedToExploring, onRevealHealthPenaltyIfMultipleWeapons, onRevealDamagePenaltyIfCharacterXpAtLeast, plusDamagePerFull10AmmoOfAttacker, onRevealWeaponDamagePenalty, onRevealBonusDamageIfCharacterDamaged, cannotBeDefeatedIf*) and returns blockedByCannotDefeat/effectiveDamage. The multi path loops the reveal/defeat/not-defeated effect hooks per card (MA-037/031 AoE, Mercenaries/Nightmare/Outbreak reveal+defeat+not-defeated, Toughness/Luck/redirect consumption, infection increases, Barry chain, Reaper, on-defeat 'may' prompts, decorations/level/XP, partner HP/death), handles MA-038/040/056o/057o and expands MA-039/072 reveals into the batch; non-Infected reveals get take/bottom prompts. Partner Modification explore fixed: partner-attached weapons join the explore (explorableWeapons + isPartnerWeapon, validation allows them, they are NOT moved to the play area / trashed / removed, and are once-per-turn via remainingWeaponUses), the leader is chosen on the explore action (action.leader, fallback partnerLeading) and the leading character takes the damage, and the pre-existing single-explore bug where a leading partner never lost Health was fixed (baseLeadingHp - damage, clamped). AI enumeration offers exploreCount 1 and all-in; client explorePicker gains exploreCountOptions, partner flags, and ActionBar renders an explore-count selector + Main/Partner 