{"ts": "2026-11-07T16:20:00", "task": "M5-T05 rules verification checklist vs the official FAQ + Gatling Gun Majini fix", "status": "ok", "note": "Verified the engine against rulebook Ch. VIII (FAQ) with a real-data probe of the explore path (PREMIER_CARDS / FIRST_TIMER_PILES, setup + applyAction); the checklist is docs/rules/FAQ-VERIFICATION.md. FAQ-1 Jill L1 + Grenade PASS (+5 per Explosive weapon used); FAQ-2 Jill L2 + Rocket Launcher PASS (Explosives go to discard, never trashed); 'do as much as you can' partial draws PASS (draw 5 from 2+0 -> 2; AC-007 with only 2 drawable -> 2). FAQ-3 Gatling Gun Majini was a real GAP: the engine added +5 per full 10 total Ammo to the PLAYER's damage, but the official FAQ ('the Gatling Gun Majini would get +30 Damage') and the Master Card List ('This infected deals +5 damage for every 10 ammo in the exploring player's play area') both say the Infected's OWN attack is boosted. Manny ruled: Infected's attack. Fixed resolveExplore (boostedAttack) and resolveMultiExplore (atk); regression tests added to explore.test.ts (single- and multi-explore). Probe after the fix: 60 Ammo + Handgun(10) vs MA-014 (40HP/30atk) -> not defeated, 60 damage taken; multi-explore [MA-014, MA-001] -> 70 taken. Gates: typecheck 0 (3 workspaces), game-core 707, server 96, client 135, vite build OK, soak 22/30 natural (floor 0.6; the pre-fix total was also 22/30)."}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T16:45:00", "task": "ActionBar: full prompt panel + fallback buttons for unhandled legal actions", "status": "ok", "note": "The ActionBar is the only prompt renderer but showed only the FIRST prompt per seat and labeled every numeric option as a seat number, so XP-amount prompts ('Remove how many XP?') rendered as 'Player 1/2/3'. Now: (1) every queued prompt for the seat renders, so chained prompts stay visible; (2) optionLabel takes the prompt kind - XP-amount kinds (we046ChooseAmount, skillRemoveXpAmount) render 'N XP', seat choices still render player names, and bare card ids resolve via cardDefs as well as instance ids; (3) a fallback 'Other actions' section renders any legal action the rest of the UI does not expose, so no legal action is unreachable - currently Outbreak attack and Alliance attachToPartner, both previously legal with NO UI. Verified in a real browser (Vite dev): an Outbreak attack with the Combat Knife dealt 5 damage to Player 2 and spent the Explore. Tests: +6 in client/src/ui/ActionBarPrompts.test.tsx (queued prompts, XP labels, seat labels, card labels, attack, attachToPartner). Gates: typecheck 0, game-core 707, server 96, client 141, vite build OK."}
