{"ts": "2026-11-07T22:29:09", "task": "Card art round 3: premier + alliance resource cards (54 PNGs)", "status": "ok", "note": "Sliced a fourth Tabletop Simulator sheet (4900x4865, 10x7 grid @ 490x695, 63 filled slots) into 54 unique per-card PNGs: AM-001..AM-004, IT-001/003/004, WE-001..WE-025 (all premier + alliance weapons), AC-001..AC-022 (all premier + alliance actions), plus CARD-BACK.png (the generic card back from slot r7c10). Several cards appeared twice on the sheet, so 63 cells collapsed to 54 unique ids; ids were read off the printed bottom-right card numbers. Quantized to 256 colours at 320px wide. CARD-ART is now 149 PNGs / 18MB; dist 19MB with 149 PNG assets. Gates: typecheck clean, client 141 (the no-art test case moved from it-001 to we-043 since IT-001 now has art), vite build OK. Browser-verified on the prod server: every resource card renders its PNG."}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T23:08:31", "task": "Fix card art rendering: restore art CSS, crop character art", "status": "ok", "note": "The art CSS block (.card-art-img absolute-fill, .card-has-art scrim rows, .card-portrait-img) had been dropped in an earlier mansion-reveal refactor, so the new PNGs rendered unstyled: resource cards showed a small image with the app's text below instead of the art filling the card, and character cards crammed the whole card scan into the portrait window (weirdly cropped). Restored the block from commit 9c67613; cropped all 51 CH-*.png to the character art window (320x260, below the [CHARACTER] banner and above the name bar); gave the portrait window an aspect-ratio of 320/260 so the art is never cropped or letterboxed; fixed the ::after 'Art' placeholder specificity; dropped the character name bar to 9px/0.5px so long names fit. Gates: typecheck clean, client 141, vite build OK. Browser-verified on prod: character art fills the window with no watermark/truncation, resource cards fill their frames."}
{"ts": "2026-11-07T23:48:53", "task": "Card art round 4: Outbreak + Nightmare + Mercenaries resources (52 PNGs)", "status": "ok", "note": "Sliced a fifth Tabletop Simulator sheet (4900x4865, 10x7 grid @ 490x695, 66 filled slots) into 52 more per-card PNGs: IN-001..IN-007 (Outbreak infection cards), AC-023..AC-041 (Outbreak + Nightmare actions), WE-026..WE-050 (Outbreak + Nightmare + Mercenaries weapons), IT-005 (First Aid Spray). Slot r7c10 is the generic card back (verified against CARD-BACK.png). Ids were read off the printed bottom-right card numbers; Mercenaries ammo/actions that also appear here were left as the round-2 files. Quantized to 256 colours at 320px wide. CARD-ART is now 201 PNGs / 27MB; dist 28MB with 201 PNG assets. Gates: typecheck clean, client 141 (the no-art test case moved again, we-043 -> ma-073), vite build OK, smoke 12/12. Browser-verified: an Outbreak pass-and-play renders the new action/weapon art."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T00:11:15", "task": "Card art round 5: promo characters PR-001..PR-010 (10 PNGs)", "status": "ok", "note": "Sliced a sixth Tabletop Simulator sheet (5500x5390, cards fill only the top 1539px: 10 cards @ 550x770 in row 1 plus CH-022 alone in row 2) into 10 promo-character PNGs PR-001..PR-010 (Chris Redfield, Jill Valentine, George Hamilton, Jim Chapman, Albert Wesker, Yoko Suzuki, Alyssa Ashcroft, Cindy Lennox, Rebecca Chambers, HUNK). CH-022 was already covered by round 1 and left alone. The promo cards have a thinner header than the base character cards, so the art crop runs from just under the [CHARACTER] banner to the torn edge above the name panel (320x292, art only; the printed NN Health badge stays in the top-right corner). Ids were read off the printed bottom-right codes one cell at a time. CARD-ART is now 211 PNGs / 28MB; dist 30MB with 211 PNG assets. Gates: typecheck clean, client 141, vite build OK. Browser-verified: a pass-and-play that drew pr-010/pr-009 renders the promo art."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T08:05:00", "task": "Greedy playout for hard bots (+ three pre-existing engine bugs it exposed)", "status": "ok", "note": "choosePlayoutAction (ai/policy.ts) replaces chooseGreedyAction for hard difficulty: 1-ply score every candidate, keep the best per candidateKind (all buys share ONE kind, or 8+ market piles fill the shortlist and crowd out the explore/play lines), then roll out the rest of the turn with the same greedy policy and compare END-OF-TURN positions (ROLLOUT_MAX_STEPS=5, ROLLOUT_CANDIDATE_CAP=6). A game-winning line scores WIN_BONUS - steps (fastest win wins) and is judged by speed alone, since leftover turn pools are worthless once the game is over. Measured on First Timer (2 hard bots, seeds 1-8): the playout agrees with the 1-ply greedy on 89% of decisions, explores LESS per turn (0.24 -> 0.14) because it declines the losing fights the EXPLORE_BIAS accepted, and roughly DOUBLES the Decorations the bots win (~14 -> ~30 per game, the metric the game is decided on). Three pre-existing engine bugs the stronger AI reached, all fixed with regression tests: (1) the Kevlar Jacket ma-054o ended up in two zones at once - applyDamageWithKevlar updates state, but four call sites rebuilt the seat from the pre-kevlar player/target (restoring it into attached) or rebuilt the pile from a stale local (dropping it into no zone); reading state.mansionBottom back into the local is wrong because the reveal lives only in the local rev.mansion. (2) WE-019's bottom reveal duplicated the revealed card the same way. (3) Stale prompt options duplicated moved cards - prompts built during one action can be answered after a second prompt already moved the chosen card, so we044/ma098/ac043/we036/we037/luisDiscardOne/chooseActionCardCostAtMost and the Rebecca L1 trash-target handler now verify the source zone first (weskerDiscardOneCard and ac044Discard already did). Tests: new ai/playout.test.ts (9: legality, determinism, no mutation, fallbacks, sequencing an ammo card before the explore it enables, declining a losing explore the 1-ply bias accepts, fastest-win), +4 rulesText regressions (kevlar single/multi/trap, WE-019 bottom), bot.test.ts hard=playout, sim.test.ts explore floor 0.15 -> 0.08 plus a Decorations floor (150). Soak ~11s -> ~127s, timeout 240s. Gates: typecheck 0 (3 workspaces), server 97, client 141, client build OK, game-core 722 (36 files, incl. the soak) green."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T09:15:00", "task": "Art-only card faces in hand + resource piles", "status": "ok", "note": "CardView gains an `artOnly` prop: when the card has art, the app's printed rows (.card-top type header + cost badge, .card-name, .card-stats/.card-bonus/.card-text) and the .card::before type band are hidden (opacity 0 / display none, still in the DOM) and fade back in on :hover. Cards without art ignore the prop. Hand.tsx and the Board's resource piles pass artOnly, so those cards now show only the artwork instead of the app's name/header/cost drawn on top of a card scan that already carries its own printed name/header/cost. The HoverCard popup already shows the full card, so the details stay one hover away. ALSO FIXED: restarted the Vite dev server - its import.meta.glob is startup-evaluated and had been serving only the round-1 art set (69 of 211 PNGs), so every card from rounds 2-5 showed the placeholder frame on :5173. Verified in the browser on the prod server: all hand + resource cards carry card-art-only, .card-top/.card-name compute to opacity 0, .card::before is display:none, and the hover-reveal rules are live in the stylesheet. Gates: typecheck 0 (3 workspaces), client 142."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T12:30:00", "task": "Custom card line: MX-001 Mr. X + lobby Custom Cards toggle", "status": "ok", "note": "First fan-designed card. Ruling (Manny): 'If this infected is not defeated, place it on top of the mansion as the 5th upcoming card' = insert into the mansion DECK 5th from the top (index 4), not the bottom and not the top. New set 'custom' + game-core/src/data/custom.ts (CUSTOM_CARDS, deliberately NOT in ALL_CARDS) + InfectedEffect kind 'onNotDefeatedInsertIntoMansionAt' + mansion.insertAt(). Reachability is a room toggle: expandable Custom Cards picker in the create-room form, the host room controls and pass & play; selection rides createRoom.customCards / setCustomCards (protocol + rooms + ws) and cardsForScenario(id, {customCards}) appends them; setup() shuffles every custom mansion card it finds in that list into the Mansion (kitchen-sink scenarios exclude them from the fallback pass and append uniformly, so both paths agree). Consumed in the single-explore, multi-explore and AC-042 deferred-explore disposition paths. Art: CARD-ART/MX-001.png from Manny's scan (320x435, 256 colours, 102 KB). MA-025 was already Alliance's Duvalia, so the custom card uses the mx- prefix. Tests: engine/customCards.test.ts (13) + protocol/rooms/hotseat/Lobby cases. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 735, server 102, client 146, vite build OK. Known limitation: a not-defeated Mr. X gets no mansion-reveal overlay (it stays in the mansion zone; detectReveal only reports attached/mansionBottom/removed) - the same pre-existing gap as Uroboros Aheri's shuffle-back."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T13:10:00", "task": "Extend the mansion-reveal overlay to re-inserted cards", "status": "ok", "note": "MX-001 Mr. X (and any card that goes back INTO the mansion deck) now gets a reveal overlay. A zone diff cannot see it - the zone never changes - so detectReveal also checks the reveal itself: the revealed cards are the top exploreCount of the PRE-explore mansionDeck, and a revealed card found back in next.mansionDeck was re-inserted. Do NOT compare deck indices: every card behind the reveal shifts up, so index drift flags cards that were never revealed. Reveal.outcomeZone gains 'mansion'; App.tsx renders 'was returned to the Mansion deck.' A defeated card in the same explore still wins (the zone-change loop runs first). Browser-verified on a forced Mr. X reveal (seed 3, top of the deck): the overlay shows his art, HP 60 / ATK 30, the printed text and the new result line. Tests: +4 in anims.test.ts (client 150); typecheck clean; vite build OK."}
{"ts": "2026-11-08T15:20:00", "task": "Custom character line: CU-001 Ricardo Irving (L1 reveal + L2 damage bargain)", "status": "ok", "note": "Second fan card and the first custom CHARACTER (80 Health, 1 copy, level1At 3 / level2At 8). L1 revealInventoryTopForAction: during your turn, reveal the top of your Inventory; an Action there moves to your hand (once per turn, needs a non-empty Inventory). L2 damageReductionAndGiveDamage (threshold 30, reduction 10, give 10): a hit ABOVE 30 is provisionally lowered by 10 and a ricardoL2 prompt asks which Character takes 10 (options = every other seat + Decline); accepting deals 10 to the chosen Character, declining re-applies the reduction so the full hit lands. Implemented as ONE choke point, applyRicardoDamage(state, seat, hp, amount) in abilities.ts, called from EVERY applyHpLoss site (actions.ts, mercenaries.ts, nightmare.ts, outbreak.ts, skill.ts) - the engine resolves damage atomically through applyHpLoss, so a helper at that seam covers explore, traps, AoE, MA-031/037/038, Kevlar and skill damage. The two applyHpLoss calls inside the ricardoL2 prompt handler are the effect itself, not damage intake. Art: CARD-ART/CU-001.png from Manny's scan, cropped to the character art window (569x462 -> 320x260, 256 colours, 57 KB). The lobby Custom Cards picker now lists characters too (hint: Infected go to the Mansion deck, Characters enter the deal pool) and selectableCharacters(room) only offers custom characters when the room enabled them. Tests: engine/customCharacters.test.ts (11) + 2 ActionBar + 1 Lobby + 1 portrait + 1 gate case. Gates: typecheck clean (3 workspaces), game-core 746, server 102, client 155, vite build OK."}
